==============================================================================
Q1 -- physics_model.generate_signal: sample-index rounding vs continuous time
==============================================================================
Code (Source/physics_model.py:23-45), quoted verbatim:
  line 32:  n_samples = int(duration * sample_rate)
  line 33:  time = np.linspace(0, duration, n_samples)
  line 36:  for beat_t in beat_times:
  line 37:      arrival_t = beat_t + tof
  line 40:      mask = (time >= arrival_t) & (time <= arrival_t + pulse_window)
  line 41:      local_t = time[mask] - arrival_t
  line 42:      pulse_shape = np.exp(-15 * local_t) * np.sin(2 * np.pi * 100 * local_t)
=> `time` is a continuous np.linspace axis (not rounded sample indices);
   `local_t` = time[mask] - arrival_t is evaluated on that continuous axis,
   i.e. the carrier IS evaluated at t-(beat_t+tof) continuously.
   The `mask` selection (time>=arrival_t) picks the nearest sample GRID points
   >= arrival_t, but the carrier phase itself is not snapped to a rounded index --
   it uses the true (non-integer-multiple) time value at each selected sample.

heart_rate_hz=1.15 (default) for all 3 classes => beat_times identical: np.arange(0,3.0,0.869565) -- SAME beat_t grid used by all classes.

healthy                kPa=  4.5  tof=8.4063ms  peak_amp=0.9590  5%thresh=0.0479  first|x|>5%peak: sample_idx=5  t=10.0067ms
significant_fibrosis   kPa=  7.5  tof=6.5115ms  peak_amp=0.9630  5%thresh=0.0482  first|x|>5%peak: sample_idx=4  t=8.0053ms
cirrhosis              kPa= 12.0  tof=5.1478ms  peak_amp=0.9340  5%thresh=0.0467  first|x|>5%peak: sample_idx=3  t=6.0040ms

Sub-sample lag between classes (parabolic-interpolated cross-correlation,
full np.correlate 'full' mode, quadratic interpolation around the discrete peak):
  healthy vs significant_fibrosis: discrete peak lag=-1 samples, sub-sample correction=0.0456 samples, total lag=-0.9544 samples = -1.9088 ms  (raw tof difference = -1.8948 ms)
  healthy vs cirrhosis: discrete peak lag=-2 samples, sub-sample correction=0.3467 samples, total lag=-1.6533 samples = -3.3065 ms  (raw tof difference = -3.2585 ms)

