Q2 -- cnn_classifier.extract_raw_windows: offset / length / count / overlap
==============================================================================
Code (Source/cnn_classifier.py:18-46), quoted verbatim:
  line 35: beat_period = 1.0 / heart_rate_hz
  line 36: beat_times = np.arange(0, duration, beat_period)
  line 40: start_idx = np.searchsorted(time, beat_t)
  line 41: end_idx = start_idx + window_size
  line 44: windows.append(signal[start_idx:end_idx])
=> window start offset from beat_t = 0 samples (window starts exactly at beat_t,
   found via searchsorted -- no additional offset applied).
=> window length = window_size default = 100 samples = 200.0 ms at 500Hz.
Windows per 3s realization at default heart rate (1.15Hz) with jitter_std=0.03, n=2000 sampled realizations: min=3, max=4, mean=3.9965
Overlap check: beat_period at hr=1.15Hz = 0.8696s, window duration = 0.2000s.
  window duration (0.2000s) < beat_period (0.8696s) => NO overlap between consecutive windows at default heart rate.
  Even at a +4sigma jittered heart rate (1.2700Hz), beat_period=0.7874s still > window duration 0.2000s => no overlap.

