==============================================================================
Q4 -- what varies within a class across realizations (Stage 3 & Stage 4)?
==============================================================================
Stage 3 loop, Source/cnn_classifier.py:81-90 (quoted above): `kpa` is the loop's
fixed dict value (stiffness_classes[name]) passed unchanged into generate_signal();
only `jittered_hr = 1.15 + np.random.normal(0, jitter_std)` varies per realization.
kPa is NEVER sampled or jittered within a class in this loop.

Stage 4 loop, Source/floor_characterization_cnn.py:48-52, quoted verbatim:
  def generate_degraded_windows(kpa, depth_m, frequency_hz, n_needed, jitter_std=0.03):
      while len(windows) < n_needed:
          jittered_hr = 1.15 + np.random.normal(0, jitter_std)
          time, clean_signal, tof = generate_signal(kpa, heart_rate_hz=jittered_hr)
Same pattern: `kpa` is a fixed function argument (unchanged per call), only
`jittered_hr` and (later in the function) additive sensor noise vary. kPa is
never sampled/jittered within a class here either.

Stage 4 (clean-CNN crosscheck), Source/noise_robustness_stress_test_clean_cnn.py:81-90,
quoted verbatim:
  def generate_windows(kpa, depth_m, frequency_hz, n_needed, noise_std, jitter_std=0.03):
      while len(windows) < n_needed:
          jittered_hr = 1.15 + np.random.normal(0, jitter_std)
          time, clean_signal, tof = generate_signal(kpa, heart_rate_hz=jittered_hr)
          attenuated, alpha = attenuate_signal(clean_signal, kpa, depth_m, frequency_hz)
          noisy = attenuated + np.random.normal(0, noise_std, size=attenuated.shape)
Same pattern again: kpa fixed, heart rate jittered, additive Gaussian sensor noise varies.
CONCLUSION: across all three generating loops inspected (Stage 3, and both Stage 4
scripts), the only per-realization randomness is heart-rate jitter (and, where present,
additive sensor noise). kPa is a constant per class, drawn once from stiffness_classes,
never resampled or jittered within a class.
